WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:17.786
My name is Zhang Mei Jin, and I am a 22-year-old silk worker living in Guangdong Province, China.

2
00:00:18.507 --> 00:00:23.629
The year is 1880 and China trades many goods worldwide, especially silk.

3
00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:29.471
Part of the Pearl River Delta is located here, which makes this area one of China's most important

4
00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:30.372
sources of silk.

5
00:00:31.052 --> 00:00:36.054
The river is rich with sand and mud, and this material fertilizes the mulberry trees.

6
00:00:36.914 --> 00:00:40.476
We use mulberry leaves to feed the silkworms that produce the silk.

7
00:00:41.216 --> 00:00:46.678
Most of the women in my village work in the silk industry, including my grandmother and mother, and

8
00:00:46.738 --> 00:00:49.940
our expertise has given us more power and independence.

9
00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.282
After all, without the women silk workers, how can our village survive?

10
00:00:56.122 --> 00:01:01.472
Chinese silk has been regarded as the best in the world for many centuries and is in high

11
00:01:01.553 --> 00:01:04.374
demand. Perhaps you know of the Silk Road?

12
00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:10.937
The Silk Road allowed our ancestors to trade many different types of goods with foreign merchants, but silk

13
00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:13.318
was always China's main commodity.

14
00:01:14.119 --> 00:01:17.020
So China guarded the secret of its silk carefully.

15
00:01:17.981 --> 00:01:23.904
Taking a silkworm out of China was forbidden, but many foreigners still tried to obtain our precious Chinese

16
00:01:23.964 --> 00:01:30.734
silkworms. Long ago the ones who tried to smuggle silkworms out of the country were executed, so it

17
00:01:30.794 --> 00:01:34.836
was many centuries before anyone learned the secret of Chinese silk.

18
00:01:36.417 --> 00:01:42.960
A silkworm is a caterpillar, and when this caterpillar becomes an adult moth, the female lays three hundred

19
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.140
to five hundred eggs.

20
00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:50.683
These eggs are so tiny that 35,000 of them weigh only 28 grams.

21
00:01:51.503 --> 00:01:57.612
As soon as the eggs hatch, the young silkworms are placed on wooden trays, and these trays are

22
00:01:57.692 --> 00:02:00.954
stacked on top of each other inside a dry farmhouse.

23
00:02:01.835 --> 00:02:07.039
Fresh, shredded mulberry leaves are sprinkled on top of the young worms, and they eat and eat.

24
00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:12.443
When I was seven years old, my job was to help pick leaves from the mulberry trees and

25
00:02:12.503 --> 00:02:14.045
fill many baskets with them.

26
00:02:14.685 --> 00:02:20.690
My mother and the other women feed the silkworms every two hours, day and night, and all you

27
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.952
hear are worms crunching on the leaves.

28
00:02:23.648 --> 00:02:25.349
The farm is quite noisy!

29
00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:32.014
The work is very hard because each worm has to be put on a new, clean tray every

30
00:02:32.094 --> 00:02:37.378
day and needs to be protected from bright light, loud noises, and strong smells.

31
00:02:38.098 --> 00:02:42.622
The worms don't like to be disturbed or they don't grow well, and when I was a young

32
00:02:42.682 --> 00:02:46.965
girl, my mother never let me even speak inside the farmhouse.

33
00:02:47.685 --> 00:02:51.228
This was difficult because I had so many questions to ask!

34
00:02:52.196 --> 00:02:58.438
After about a month of eating, resting, and shedding their skin four times, the silkworms are ready to

35
00:02:58.518 --> 00:02:59.638
spin their cocoons.

36
00:03:00.458 --> 00:03:06.220
This is when the workers put them on spinning racks, and the silkworm builds its cocoon by making

37
00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.981
a long fiber and surrounding itself with it.

38
00:03:09.721 --> 00:03:13.162
In about three days, the silkworms look like white balls.

39
00:03:14.002 --> 00:03:20.424
Then, eight to ten days later, the cocoons are ready to be unwound, a process called reeling.

40
00:03:21.076 --> 00:03:25.158
Right now I am still being trained by one of my aunts to unwind the cocoons.

41
00:03:25.958 --> 00:03:31.100
My job is to reel the silk threads onto a large spinning wheel, but we have a machine

42
00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.321
that helps us to do this.

43
00:03:33.161 --> 00:03:38.363
Our reeling machine is built directly over a large pot of very hot water, and I put the

44
00:03:38.423 --> 00:03:40.704
cocoons in the pot to kill the worms inside.

45
00:03:41.584 --> 00:03:47.687
A long wooden plank, placed across the pot, has two poles that have two small rollers attached, and

46
00:03:47.747 --> 00:03:50.088
a bamboo tube hangs from each roller.

47
00:03:50.812 --> 00:03:55.394
As I stir the cocoons in the hot water, the ends of the silk fibers float free.

48
00:03:56.134 --> 00:04:02.276
I grab the ends of the threads, gently pull and twist them together, and feed these fibers through

49
00:04:02.316 --> 00:04:03.256
the bamboo tube.

50
00:04:04.356 --> 00:04:08.958
Then the fibers wind around the rollers and onto a large reeling wheel.

51
00:04:09.618 --> 00:04:14.920
When the fiber of the cocoon is completely unwound, only the dead insect is left.

52
00:04:16.004 --> 00:04:21.889
Silk reeling is very tricky, and it takes years of experience to learn how to do it just

53
00:04:22.069 --> 00:04:29.215
right. One silkworm can make a strand of silk about one thousand meters long—the longer the strand, the

54
00:04:29.255 --> 00:04:29.995
better the silk.

55
00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:34.319
If a strand is too short, the quality of the silk suffers.

56
00:04:34.919 --> 00:04:42.646
Remember, the best-quality silk thread is one that is reeled continuously in one long strand, which means I

57
00:04:42.686 --> 00:04:45.348
cannot break the fragile thread as I am handling it.

58
00:04:46.128 --> 00:04:52.191
I have heard that automatic machines powered by steam are being used now because they can reel many

59
00:04:52.251 --> 00:04:55.812
cocoons at a time and unwind the silk more quickly.

60
00:04:56.632 --> 00:05:01.995
Businessmen are building large factories near cities and employing hundreds of women to work in them.

61
00:05:02.915 --> 00:05:08.837
But these factories are very noisy and some silk workers have gotten injured using the machines.

62
00:05:09.538 --> 00:05:13.779
Many of our friends and neighbors have left our village to find work in the factories.

63
00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:20.606
We miss them, but my family is content to stay here and stick to the older traditions because

64
00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:23.467
we take pride in quality more than quantity.

65
00:05:25.028 --> 00:05:31.251
In my village silk making is so much more than just making a profit; we view our work

66
00:05:31.391 --> 00:05:33.072
as a spiritual exercise.

67
00:05:33.852 --> 00:05:40.615
Whether it is collecting the cocoons, unwinding the threads, or even spinning the silk, each movement is done

68
00:05:40.715 --> 00:05:42.556
precisely and slowly.

69
00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:50.045
This is why the Chinese martial art tai chi chuan includes exercises from silk-reeling techniques.

70
00:05:50.865 --> 00:06:01.012
Practicing tai chi silk-reeling exercises helps a person to move slowly, smoothly, evenly, and continuously, and prepares the

71
00:06:01.072 --> 00:06:03.954
body to make gentle yet accurate movements.

72
00:06:04.635 --> 00:06:10.419
We are totally dedicated to our art, so it is not surprising that the silk from Guangdong is

73
00:06:10.459 --> 00:06:11.920
considered to be superior.

74
00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:18.203
Making silk is a unique tradition of my village, my people, and my country.

75
00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:23.507
I am proud it is part of my heritage and hope that one day I can learn all

76
00:06:23.547 --> 00:06:26.229
the skills needed to become a proficient silk worker.

77
00:06:26.909 --> 00:06:32.873
Sadly the way silk is being made is changing, but I hope that silk making will always be

78
00:06:32.933 --> 00:06:37.176
considered a noble art and that one day my children will learn it too.
